Lab 17: Using YAML for Cluster and Policy Configuration
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

• Write YAML definitions for clusters in Red Hat Advanced Cluster Management (RHACM) • Create policy configurations using YAML syntax • Define placement rules for cluster management • Apply YAML configurations using the OpenShift CLI (oc) • Test and validate YAML-based cluster and policy configurations • Troubleshoot common YAML configuration issues in RHACM environments

