Task 1: Create YAML Files for Cluster Definitions
Subtask 1.1: Understanding Cluster YAML Structure
First, let's examine the basic structure of a cluster definition in RHACM.

Access your lab environment and open a terminal

Create a working directory for your YAML files:

mkdir -p ~/rhacm-lab17
cd ~/rhacm-lab17
Create a basic cluster definition file:
cat > managed-cluster-dev.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: cluster.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: ManagedCluster
metadata:
  name: dev-cluster-01
  namespace: dev-cluster-01
  labels:
    environment: development
    region: us-east-1
    cluster.open-cluster-management.io/clusterset: development
spec:
  hubAcceptsClient: true
  leaseDurationSeconds: 60
EOF
Create a cluster namespace definition:
cat > cluster-namespace-dev.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: dev-cluster-01
  labels:
    cluster.open-cluster-management.io/managedCluster: dev-cluster-01
EOF
Subtask 1.2: Creating Production Cluster Configuration
Create a production cluster definition with enhanced security settings:
cat > managed-cluster-prod.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: cluster.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: ManagedCluster
metadata:
  name: prod-cluster-01
  namespace: prod-cluster-01
  labels:
    environment: production
    region: us-west-2
    cluster.open-cluster-management.io/clusterset: production
    security-level: high
spec:
  hubAcceptsClient: true
  leaseDurationSeconds: 30
  managedClusterClientConfigs:
  - url: https://prod-cluster-01.example.com:6443
    caBundle: LS0tLS1CRUdJTi...
EOF
Create the corresponding namespace:
cat > cluster-namespace-prod.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: prod-cluster-01
  labels:
    cluster.open-cluster-management.io/managedCluster: prod-cluster-01
    environment: production
EOF
Subtask 1.3: Creating ClusterSet Configuration
Define a cluster set for grouping related clusters:
cat > clusterset-development.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: cluster.open-cluster-management.io/v1beta2
kind: ManagedClusterSet
metadata:
  name: development
spec:
  clusterSelector:
    selectorType: ExclusiveClusterSetLabel
EOF
Create a production cluster set:
cat > clusterset-production.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: cluster.open-cluster-management.io/v1beta2
kind: ManagedClusterSet
metadata:
  name: production
spec:
  clusterSelector:
    selectorType: ExclusiveClusterSetLabel
EOF
Task 2: Create YAML Files for Policy Definitions
Subtask 2.1: Security Policy Configuration
Create a namespace policy to ensure required namespaces exist:
cat > policy-namespace-security.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: Policy
metadata:
  name: policy-namespace-security
  namespace: default
  annotations:
    policy.open-cluster-management.io/standards: NIST-CSF
    policy.open-cluster-management.io/categories: PR.AC Identity Management Authentication and Access Control
    policy.open-cluster-management.io/controls: PR.AC-4
spec:
  remediationAction: enforce
  disabled: false
  policy-templates:
    - objectDefinition:
        apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
        kind: ConfigurationPolicy
        metadata:
          name: policy-namespace-security
        spec:
          remediationAction: enforce
          severity: high
          namespaceSelector:
            exclude:
              - kube-*
            include:
              - default
          object-templates:
            - complianceType: musthave
              objectDefinition:
                kind: Namespace
                apiVersion: v1
                metadata:
                  name: security-monitoring
                  labels:
                    security.policy: enforced
EOF
Create a pod security policy:
cat > policy-pod-security.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: Policy
metadata:
  name: policy-pod-security-standards
  namespace: default
  annotations:
    policy.open-cluster-management.io/standards: NIST SP 800-53
    policy.open-cluster-management.io/categories: SC System and Communications Protection
    policy.open-cluster-management.io/controls: SC-28
spec:
  remediationAction: inform
  disabled: false
  policy-templates:
    - objectDefinition:
        apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
        kind: ConfigurationPolicy
        metadata:
          name: policy-pod-security-standards
        spec:
          remediationAction: inform
          severity: medium
          namespaceSelector:
            exclude:
              - kube-*
              - openshift-*
            include:
              - "*"
          object-templates:
            - complianceType: musthave
              objectDefinition:
                apiVersion: v1
                kind: Pod
                metadata:
                  namespace: default
                spec:
                  securityContext:
                    runAsNonRoot: true
                    runAsUser: 1000
                    fsGroup: 2000
EOF
Subtask 2.2: Resource Management Policy
Create a resource quota policy:
cat > policy-resource-quota.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: Policy
metadata:
  name: policy-resource-quota
  namespace: default
  annotations:
    policy.open-cluster-management.io/standards: Custom
    policy.open-cluster-management.io/categories: Resource Management
    policy.open-cluster-management.io/controls: Quota-1
spec:
  remediationAction: enforce
  disabled: false
  policy-templates:
    - objectDefinition:
        apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
        kind: ConfigurationPolicy
        metadata:
          name: policy-resource-quota
        spec:
          remediationAction: enforce
          severity: medium
          namespaceSelector:
            include:
              - development
              - testing
          object-templates:
            - complianceType: musthave
              objectDefinition:
                apiVersion: v1
                kind: ResourceQuota
                metadata:
                  name: compute-quota
                spec:
                  hard:
                    requests.cpu: "4"
                    requests.memory: 8Gi
                    limits.cpu: "8"
                    limits.memory: 16Gi
                    persistentvolumeclaims: "10"
EOF
Subtask 2.3: Network Policy Configuration
Create a network security policy:
cat > policy-network-security.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: Policy
metadata:
  name: policy-network-security
  namespace: default
  annotations:
    policy.open-cluster-management.io/standards: NIST-CSF
    policy.open-cluster-management.io/categories: PR.AC Network Security
    policy.open-cluster-management.io/controls: PR.AC-5
spec:
  remediationAction: inform
  disabled: false
  policy-templates:
    - objectDefinition:
        apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
        kind: ConfigurationPolicy
        metadata:
          name: policy-network-security
        spec:
          remediationAction: inform
          severity: high
          namespaceSelector:
            include:
              - production
          object-templates:
            - complianceType: musthave
              objectDefinition:
                apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
                kind: NetworkPolicy
                metadata:
                  name: deny-all-ingress
                spec:
                  podSelector: {}
                  policyTypes:
                  - Ingress
EOF
Task 3: Create YAML Files for Placement Rules
Subtask 3.1: Basic Placement Rule Configuration
Create a development environment placement rule:
cat > placement-rule-dev.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: apps.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: PlacementRule
metadata:
  name: placement-dev-clusters
  namespace: default
spec:
  clusterSelector:
    matchLabels:
      environment: development
  clusterReplicas: 2
  clusterConditions:
    - status: "True"
      type: ManagedClusterConditionAvailable
EOF
Create a production placement rule with advanced criteria:
cat > placement-rule-prod.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: apps.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: PlacementRule
metadata:
  name: placement-prod-clusters
  namespace: default
spec:
  clusterSelector:
    matchLabels:
      environment: production
      security-level: high
    matchExpressions:
      - key: region
        operator: In
        values:
          - us-west-2
          - us-east-1
  clusterReplicas: 1
  clusterConditions:
    - status: "True"
      type: ManagedClusterConditionAvailable
  schedulerName: default-scheduler
EOF
Subtask 3.2: Advanced Placement Configuration
Create a placement rule with resource requirements:
cat > placement-rule-resources.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: apps.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: PlacementRule
metadata:
  name: placement-high-resource-clusters
  namespace: default
spec:
  clusterSelector:
    matchExpressions:
      - key: node-role.kubernetes.io/worker
        operator: Exists
      - key: cluster-resource-level
        operator: In
        values:
          - high
          - medium
  clusterReplicas: 3
  clusterConditions:
    - status: "True"
      type: ManagedClusterConditionAvailable
  resourceHint:
    type: cpu
    order: largest
EOF
Create a placement rule using the new Placement API:
cat > placement-new-api.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: cluster.open-cluster-management.io/v1beta1
kind: Placement
metadata:
  name: placement-new-api-example
  namespace: default
spec:
  numberOfClusters: 2
  clusterSets:
    - development
    - production
  predicates:
    - requiredClusterSelector:
        labelSelector:
          matchLabels:
            environment: development
        claimSelector:
          matchLabels:
            region.open-cluster-management.io/us-east-1: ""
  prioritizerPolicy:
    mode: Exact
    configurations:
      - scoreCoordinate:
          type: BuiltIn
          builtIn: ResourceAllocatableCPU
        weight: 1
EOF
